    {
      "@id": "xw:fw-CREAM",
      "dcterms:bibliographicCitation": "Hollnagel, E. (1998). Cognitive Reliability and Error Analysis Method (CREAM). Oxford: Elsevier Science.",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:ExternalFramework"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "The nine CPC labels used here were transcribed from an open-access secondary source (Shirali et al. 2019, MethodsX) because the book text was not consulted directly. See ../docs/PROVENANCE.md.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "rdfs:label": {
        "@value": "CREAM",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "hollnagel1998"
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:fw-HFACS",
      "dcterms:bibliographicCitation": "Shappell, S.A. & Wiegmann, D.A. (2000). The Human Factors Analysis and Classification System--HFACS. DOT/FAA/AM-00/7. Revised taxonomy as figured in Shappell et al. (2006), DOT/FAA/AM-06/18.",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:ExternalFramework"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "Two versions matter here. The 2000 report subdivides Preconditions into Substandard Conditions and Substandard Practices of Operators. The revised taxonomy figured in the 2006 report uses Environmental Factors, Condition of Operators and Personnel Factors. The crosswalk maps to the revised taxonomy and says so.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "rdfs:label": {
        "@value": "HFACS",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": [
        "shappell2000",
        "shappell2006"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:fw-HSE-PIF",
      "dcterms:bibliographicCitation": "Health and Safety Executive. Performance Influencing Factors (PIFs). HSE human factors guidance, https://www.hse.gov.uk/humanfactors/assets/docs/pifs.pdf",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:ExternalFramework"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "HSE states of its own list: 'NB. This list is not exhaustive'.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "rdfs:label": {
        "@value": "HSE Performance Influencing Factors",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "hse_pifs"
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:fw-IDHEAS-G",
      "dcterms:bibliographicCitation": "U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission (2021). The General Methodology of an Integrated Human Event Analysis System (IDHEAS-G). NUREG-2198.",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:ExternalFramework"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:label": {
        "@value": "IDHEAS-G",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "nureg2198"
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:fw-SPARH",
      "dcterms:bibliographicCitation": "Gertman, D.I., Blackman, H.S., Marble, J.L., Byers, J.C. & Smith, C.L. (2005). The SPAR-H Human Reliability Analysis Method. NUREG/CR-6883, INL/EXT-05-00509.",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:ExternalFramework"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:label": {
        "@value": "SPAR-H",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "gertman2005"
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-cream-TimeOfDay",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents time of day or circadian phase. IDHEAS-G has no such\nPIF either, so the gap is inherited rather than introduced. This is the gap that\nmatters most for shift-based occupational settings, and closing it would require\nan exposure denominator by hour of shift that no public dataset currently\nsupplies (Hanecke et al. 1998; Folkard and Tucker 2003).",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": [
        "folkard2003",
        "hanecke1998",
        "hollnagel1998"
      ],
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:cream-TimeOfDay"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-hfacs-FailedToCorrectProblem",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents a supervisor's failure to correct a known deficiency.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "shappell2000",
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:hfacs-FailedToCorrectProblem"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-hfacs-PersonalReadiness",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents personal readiness in the HFACS sense: an\nindividual's off-duty preparation for work, including rest, diet and compliance\nwith alcohol and self-medication rules. The gap is inherited rather than\nintroduced. IDHEAS-G has no fitness-for-duty PIF, whereas SPAR-H does, and the\ntwenty factors here are IDHEAS-G's twenty adopted unchanged. ehs:MentalFatigue\nis the nearest local factor and is deliberately not aligned to this one: fatigue\nis a state during the task, personal readiness is conduct before it, and one\ncauses the other rather than being it.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": [
        "gertman2005",
        "nureg2198",
        "shappell2000",
        "shappell2006"
      ],
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:hfacs-PersonalReadiness"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-hfacs-SupervisoryViolations",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents wilful supervisory disregard of rules.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "shappell2000",
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:hfacs-SupervisoryViolations"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-hse-Motivation",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents motivation or competing priorities as an attribute of the individual.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "hse_pifs",
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:hse-Motivation"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-hse-OrganisationalLearning",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents the effectiveness of organisational learning.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "hse_pifs",
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:hse-OrganisationalLearning"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "xw:gap-hse-PeerPressure",
      "rdf:type": [
        {
          "@id": "owl:NamedIndividual"
        },
        {
          "@id": "ehs:CoverageGap"
        }
      ],
      "rdfs:comment": {
        "@value": "No local factor represents peer pressure. Team and organisation factors is too coarse to stand in for it.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "ehs:sourceRef": "hse_pifs",
      "ehs:uncoveredFactor": {
        "@id": "xw:hse-PeerPressure"
      }
